# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The context is the whole workspace, because both images build from the monorepo root — a pnpm workspace
# cannot be installed from one package's directory alone. Excluding build output and local state keeps the
# context small and, more importantly, keeps a stale local `dist/` or `.next/` from being copied in and
# shadowing what the builder produces.

# Dependencies and build output — always rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated graphs. A container writes its own into a volume; copying a host one in would ship whichever
# repository happened to be scanned locally.
.traceiq
**/.traceiq
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal

# Local environment. `.env.example` is committed and copied; `.env` is the user's and is read by Compose,
# never baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and editor state.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Tests and coverage add nothing to a runtime image.
coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.test-helper.ts

# The deployment layer itself, except what an image genuinely needs.
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
